<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Spark Match Lens</title>
<style>
{{ css|safe }}
mark { background: var(--mark); color: inherit; padding: 0 2px; border-radius: 3px; }
.tier { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 650; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }
.tier.strong { color: var(--good); background: var(--good-bg); } .tier.worth { color: var(--series-1); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--series-1); }
.tier.stretch { color: var(--proxy); background: var(--proxy-bg); } .tier.none { color: var(--ink-2); }
.lbl.adjacent { color: var(--series-1); }
.unit { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); }
.note { display: block; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 2px; }
.tiers { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 16px; align-items: center; margin: 4px 0 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); }
.flag { font-weight: 650; color: var(--bad); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Spark · Step 2 · Match Lens engine (F4–F7){% if v1 %} · amended run A1{% endif %}</h1>
<p class="sub">Evidence units → multilingual retrieval → structured judge → fixed tier rules. No match score is shown to anyone; retrieval
similarity is used internally only to pick each outcome's top 3 units. Every tier is explained by quotes or a stated reason. Method
pre-registered in <span class="mono">docs/method.md §6</span>; changes made after results are listed in its dated note.</p>
{% if v1 %}<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:8px"><h3>Registered run (v1) and amendment A1 (v2)</h3>
<p class="muted" style="margin:0">This page shows the amended run v2: ESCO descriptions in the extraction prompt (A1.1), the §1 rule-(c)
example in the judge prompt (A1.2), and no adjacency through hub skills (A1.3). The registered run v1 stays the registered result and is
shown beside it. Thresholds did not move. A1 was motivated by v1's golden-set results, so v2 numbers on the golden set are optimistic.
Hub skills under A1.3 (tagged on more than 1/8 of pool units): <b>{{ hubs|join(', ') if hubs else 'none' }}</b>.
{% if v1_missed %}Missed in v1: {{ v1_missed|join('; ') }}.{% endif %}</p></div>{% endif %}

{% if a1 and not v1 %}<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:8px"><h3>Amendment A1: attempted, not completed</h3>
<p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 6px">{{ a1.status }} Preliminary pool-wide results, reported as they came out (no golden-set or F7
result exists for A1):</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Registered v1</th><th>A1 (partial)</th><th>Threshold</th></tr>
{% for name, x in a1.measures.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td>{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * x.v1) }}%</td><td>{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * x.value) }}%{% if x.value < x.threshold %} <span class="flag">below</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="kind">≥ {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * x.threshold) }}%</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="muted" style="margin:6px 0 0">A1.1 (ESCO descriptions in the extraction prompt) raised precision a little and cost recall more. Hub skills under A1 tags: {{ a1.hubs|join(', ') }}.</p></div>{% endif %}

<h2>Hard gates</h2>
{% if stale %}<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px"><span class="pill pending">STALE</span> Gate statuses predate the current engine outputs or tests; run <span class="mono">make verify</span>.</div>{% endif %}
<div class="card scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Check</th><th>Status</th></tr>
{% for label, s in gates %}<tr><td>{{ label }}</td><td><span class="pill {{ s }}">{{ s|upper }}</span></td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>

<h2>Targets</h2>
<div class="card scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Target</th><th>Kind</th><th>Status</th><th>Value</th>{% if v1 %}<th>Registered v1</th>{% endif %}</tr>
{% for name, t in targets.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="kind">{{ t.kind }}</td>
  <td>{% if t.kind == 'sensitivity' %}<span class="kind">no threshold</span>
      {% elif t.pass is none %}<span class="pill pending">N/A</span>
      {% elif not t.pass %}<span class="pill fail">MISSED</span>
      {% elif t.kind == 'proxy' %}<span class="pill proxy">PROXY · HUMAN PENDING</span>
      {% else %}<span class="pill pass">MET</span>{% endif %}</td>
  <td class="muted">{% if t.value is not none %}{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.value) }}%{% else %}n/a{% endif %}{% if t.threshold is not none %} ({{ t.op }} {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.threshold) }}%){% endif %}, n = {{ t.n }}{% if t.ci %}, 95% CI {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.ci[0]) }}–{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.ci[1]) }}%{% endif %}{% if t.kind == 'proxy' %}{{ ' · meets threshold on proxy labels' if t.pass else ' · proxy, human labels pending' }}{% endif %}
    {% if t.note %}<span class="note">{{ t.note }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
  {% if v1 %}{% set o = v1.get(name) %}<td class="muted">{% if o and o.value is not none %}{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * o.value) }}%, n = {{ o.n }}{% if o.pass is false %} · <span class="flag">missed</span>{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>{% endif %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">Kind <b>proxy</b>: the reference is AI-proxy annotator consensus or planted labels, so the result is never shown as green
(method.md, condition kinds). Kind <b>sensitivity</b>: reported for context, without a threshold. 95% CIs: bootstrap, 2,000 resamples,
seed 11 (method.md §3), items resampled independently.</p></div>
{% if meta %}<p class="muted">{{ n_stories }} stories → {{ n_units }} evidence units · {{ meta.llm_calls }} uncached LLM calls, ${{ meta.llm_usd }} spent · served by {{ meta.served_by|join(', ') }} · {{ meta.refusals }} refusals · {{ meta.units_invalid_dropped }} non-verbatim units dropped · {{ meta.judge_rejected }} judge items rejected · embeddings {{ meta.embedding }}{% if meta.tokens %} · tokens: {{ meta.tokens.input_tokens }} input, {{ meta.tokens.output_tokens }} output, {{ meta.tokens.cache_read_input_tokens }} cache read, {{ meta.tokens.cache_creation_input_tokens }} cache write{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}

{% if missed %}<h2>Missed targets and mitigation</h2>
{% for name, t in missed.items() %}<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
  <h3>{{ name }} · <span class="flag">missed</span>: {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.value) }}% against {{ t.op }} {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.threshold) }}% (n = {{ t.n }}{% if t.ci %}, 95% CI {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.ci[0]) }}–{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * t.ci[1]) }}%{% endif %})</h3>
  {% if t.note %}<p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 6px">{{ t.note }}</p>{% endif %}
  <p style="margin:0">{{ t.mitigation }}</p>
</div>{% endfor %}{% endif %}

<h2>Match Lens · NordSense (N-014) × the three running-example candidates</h2>
<p class="muted">Candidates are shown by id and a persona from the challenge's running example; no name, nationality or school is shown.</p>
{% for h in heroes %}
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:16px">
  <h3>{{ h.cid }} · {{ h.persona }}{% if h.thin %} <span class="pill pending">thin story: human follow-up</span>{% endif %}</h3>
  <div class="tiers">
    <span>Engine{% if v1 %} (v2){% endif %}: <span class="tier {{ h.pair.tier }}">{{ h.pair.tier_label }}</span></span>
    {% if h.v1 %}<span>Registered v1: <span class="tier {{ h.v1 }}">{{ tier_text[h.v1] }}</span></span>{% endif %}
    <span>Spec expects: <span class="tier {{ h.expected }}">{{ tier_text[h.expected] }}</span>{% if h.vs_spec != 'agrees' %} <span class="flag">≠ {{ h.vs_spec }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
    {% if h.consensus %}<span>Annotator consensus: <span class="tier {{ h.consensus }}">{{ tier_text[h.consensus] }}</span>{% if h.vs_consensus != 'agrees' %} <span class="flag">≠ {{ h.vs_consensus }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 8px">{{ h.pair.why }} · {{ h.n_units }} evidence unit{{ 's' if h.n_units != 1 }}</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <tr><th>Outcome</th><th>Prio</th><th>Engine</th><th>Consensus</th><th>Evidence (quote highlighted inside its unit)</th><th>Why</th></tr>
    {% for r in h.rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.outcome }}</td><td class="kind">{{ r.priority }}</td><td><span class="lbl {{ r.support }}">{{ r.support }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="lbl {{ r.consensus }}">{{ r.consensus }}</span>{% if r.consensus != r.support and r.consensus != '—' and not (r.support == 'adjacent' and r.consensus == 'none') %} <span class="flag">≠</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="unit" dir="auto">{% if r.parts[1] %}{{ r.parts[0] }}<mark>{{ r.parts[1] }}</mark>{{ r.parts[2] }}{% elif r.path %}{{ r.parts[0] }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="muted">{% if r.path %}Judge: {{ r.judge_reason }}<span class="note">Adjacent skill path: {{ r.path.from }} ({{ r.path.relation }}) {{ r.path.to }}, from unit {{ r.path.unit_id }}</span>{% else %}{{ r.reason }}{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">≠ marks an engine label that differs from consensus. Annotators do not label adjacency, so <i>adjacent</i> next to consensus <i>none</i> is expected, not flagged.</p>
</div>
{% else %}<div class="card"><span class="pill pending">PENDING</span> The engine has not run yet.</div>{% endfor %}

<h2>Golden set: engine tier vs annotator-consensus tier</h2>
{% if golden %}<div class="card scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Pair</th><th>Need</th><th>Cand.</th><th>Lang</th><th>Style</th><th>Consensus tier</th><th>Engine tier</th><th>Agreement</th>{% if v1 %}<th>Registered v1</th>{% endif %}</tr>
{% for g in golden %}<tr class="{{ 'disagree' if g.engine != g.consensus }}"><td class="mono">{{ g.pair_id }}</td><td class="mono">{{ g.need }}</td><td class="mono">{{ g.cand }}</td>
<td class="mono">{{ g.lang }}</td><td class="kind">{{ g.style }}</td><td><span class="tier {{ g.consensus }}">{{ tier_text[g.consensus] }}</span></td>
<td><span class="tier {{ g.engine }}">{{ tier_text[g.engine] }}</span></td><td>{% if g.agree == 'agrees' %}agrees{% else %}<span class="flag">≠ {{ g.agree }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% if v1 %}<td>{% if g.v1 %}<span class="tier {{ g.v1 }}">{{ tier_text[g.v1] }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endif %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table><p class="muted">Consensus tiers use direct labels only (annotators do not label adjacency, method.md §1); the engine adds ESCO adjacency.</p></div>
{% else %}<div class="card"><span class="pill pending">PENDING</span></div>{% endif %}

{% if xf %}<h2>Sensitivity X1: non-Claude annotators</h2>
<div class="card">
<p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 8px">Both golden annotators and the judge are Claude models. Two other model families blind-labelled the frozen
golden set with the original instructions: {{ xf.models.kimi }} and {{ xf.models.deepseek }} (Verda Inference). Nothing frozen changed;
no thresholds apply. These are still AI annotators, not humans.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div><h3>Agreement between annotators (Cohen's κ, 60 labels)</h3><table>
{% for name, x in xf.kappa.items() %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="mono">{{ '%.2f'|format(x.kappa) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
<div><h3>Judge (registered v1) label accuracy by reference</h3><table>
{% for name, x in xf['judge v1 (registered)'].items() if name != 'F7 vs cross-family tiers' %}<tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="mono">{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * x.accuracy) }}% (n = {{ x.n }})</td></tr>{% endfor %}
{% set f7 = xf['judge v1 (registered)']['F7 vs cross-family tiers'] %}
<tr><td>F7 tier agreement vs cross-family tiers</td><td class="mono">exact {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * f7.exact) }}%, within one {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * f7.within_one) }}% (n = {{ f7.n_pairs }} pairs)</td></tr>
<tr><td>False "supported" vs cross-family reference</td><td class="mono">{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * xf['judge v1 (registered)']['cross-family reference'].false_supported) }}% (n = {{ xf['judge v1 (registered)']['cross-family reference'].false_supported_n }})</td></tr>
</table></div></div>
<p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">Cross-family reference = the {{ xf.cross_family_reference.n }} labels where Kimi and DeepSeek agree ({{ xf.cross_family_reference.excluded_disagreements }} excluded).
Realism: Kimi rated {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * xf.realism_plausible.kimi.share) }}% and DeepSeek {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * xf.realism_plausible.deepseek.share) }}% of the 20 stories plausible.
{{ xf.cost.calls }} calls, about ${{ xf.cost.usd_estimate }} (Verda list prices).
Reading: the judge agrees about as well with the non-Claude annotators as with the Claude ones, so F6 is not mainly a same-family effect;
the F7 miss stays, because it comes from adjacency, not from who labelled.</p>
</div>{% endif %}
</main>
</body>
</html>
